## Methodology

This project uses the stage-gate methodology defined in:
- [`wiki/config/methodology.yaml`](wiki/config/methodology.yaml) — 9 models, 5 universal stages, ALLOWED/FORBIDDEN per stage, gates, end conditions
- [`wiki/config/sdlc-profile.yaml`](wiki/config/sdlc-profile.yaml) — `{{sdlc_profile}}` profile (right-sized per project tier)
- [`wiki/config/domain-profile.yaml`](wiki/config/domain-profile.yaml) — `{{domain_profile}}` profile (gate-command + path-pattern overrides)
- [`wiki/config/methodology-profile.yaml`](wiki/config/methodology-profile.yaml) — `{{methodology_profile}}` profile (process style)

These four files are **copied from the second brain** at `{{second_brain_path}}/wiki/config/` per Adoption Guide step 1. Adapt per project (artifacts, gate commands, commit scope, directory layout); keep the invariants (stage names, stage ordering, readiness ranges, hierarchy rules, work-loop structure).

**5 universal stages:**

| Stage | Readiness | ALLOWED outputs | FORBIDDEN outputs | Gate |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| **document** | 0–25% | wiki-page, raw notes, research notes | code-file, test-file | Page exists with Summary + gaps identified |
| **design** | 25–50% | design-document, ADR, tech-spec, type sketches in docs | code-file, test-file | Spec reviewed; no code yet |
| **scaffold** | 50–80% | type-definition, schema, test-stub, config-file | implementation, real test assertions | Types compile, no business logic |
| **implement** | 80–95% | implementation, integration-wiring, config | new test files | Code compiles, lint passes |
| **test** | 95–100% | test-implementation, test-results | new features, scope changes | 0 test failures, health check clean |

**Stage rules:**
- "Continue" = advance within CURRENT stage. NEVER skip ahead.
- One commit per stage. Don't advance without the stage's quality gate passing.
- ALLOWED/FORBIDDEN are not suggestions — they are hard constraints.

**Backlog hierarchy:** Epic → Module → Task. Readiness flows upward (task readiness aggregates to module, module to epic). Status flows upward. You work on tasks, not on epics directly.

**Quality gate commands per stage:**

| Stage | Gate command (this project) |
|---|---|
| document | {{gate_command_document}} |
| design | {{gate_command_design}} |
| scaffold | {{gate_command_scaffold}} |
| implement | {{gate_command_implement}} |
| test | {{gate_command_test}} |

**Work loop expectation:** the agent follows the work loop defined in `methodology-profile.yaml`. Stage boundaries are hard. ALLOWED/FORBIDDEN per stage is enforced.

